deadman is a dead man's switch: jobs ping a URL of their own when they
run, and deadman sends mail when the pings stop. It does the core of
what healthchecks.io does, with the base system: httpd(8) and slowcgi(8)
take the pings, cron(8) runs the checks, and smtpd(8) sends the mail.
There is no daemon and no database.

Each check has a period and a grace time, and is new, up, late or down.
A job can also report that it has started, so that a run that hangs
counts as down, or that it has failed.

The ping recorder is static and runs in httpd's chroot. It accepts only
well-formed tokens, and can do nothing but set the modification time of
a file that deadman made for a configured check. The checker reads its
configuration as root and then drops privileges. Both use pledge(2) and
unveil(2).
